# harmony-base — implementation roadmap

Legend: [ ] - Not implemented; [/] - Partially implemented; [x] - Fully implemented.

`harmony-base` is the first, incomplete implementation of the Harmony language
(extension `.harmony`), written **in c2x-seed** (`.c2`). It is not the full
language: it is the smallest compiler that can lex, parse, check, and emit
working code for the v0 core feature set. The full rewrite (`src/harmony`, self
hosted) comes after. Milestone: `harmony` output is **byte deterministic**.

Priority note (from AGENTS.md): **write the LLVM backend first.** The C11
backend is a debugging aid, not the goal.

Phase ordering (do not skip backwards dependencies):

| Phase | Theme | Depends on |
|---|---|---|
| P0 | Toolchain + skeleton + test harness | c2x-seed built |
| P1 | Diagnostics + source manager | P0 |
| P2 | Lexer | P1 |
| P3 | AST + Parser | P2 |
| P4 | Name resolution | P3 |
| P5 | Type checker + copy rules | P4 |
| P6 | HIR → MIR lowering | P5 |
| P7 | Exhaustiveness | P5 |
| P8 | Dataflow: init + moves | P6 |
| P9 | Borrow checker + `life` | P8 |
| P10 | Drop insertion | P9 |
| P11 | LLVM backend (priority) | P10 |
| P12 | Runtime library | P11 |
| P13 | C11 backend (secondary) | P10 |
| P14 | Reporting polish (JSON, explain, fix-its) | P2 onward |
| P15 | Fuzzing + determinism hardening | P11 |

Detailed per-subsystem checklist lives in `todo.md` under
"harmony-base — detailed implementation checklist".

## Seed capabilities to rely on (c2x-seed)

- 64-bit `int`, 8-bit `char`, pointers, `char*` strings, fixed/2D/VLA arrays.
- Named structs, struct pointers, struct arrays, struct params, struct returns
  (hidden-pointer ABI; no nested/recursive struct-returning calls).
- Globals, `extern`, forward decls, `const`, compound assign, `++/--`, `for`,
  `break`/`continue`, `switch`-less dispatch (use `if`/`else` chains).
- `asm()` for the raw syscall seam.
- **Missing** (work around): no function pointers, no `enum`, no `typedef`, no
  floats, no `unsigned`, no `switch`. Use struct-tagged values + `if`/`else`
  dispatch, and `char*` for all dynamic buffers.
